{#-
  The operator's Claude settings, reconciled against what faramir ships.

  Two edits in one pass, because both rewrite the same file and a second task
  would be working from a copy the first had already replaced:

    the deny rules faramir ships are unioned in, so a rule added upstream
    reaches the operator instead of sitting in settings.json.dist unread

    every faramir-guard hook is taken out, the guard being per project now

  Rebuilt rather than patched: a matcher whose only hook was the guard is
  dropped, and the "hooks" key goes with it when nothing else used it, so what
  is left is not an empty object that reads as a configuration someone chose.

  A hook entry with no command is kept. Only an entry naming faramir-guard is
  this role's to remove. Nothing is ever taken out of deny: the union only adds,
  so a rule the operator wrote themselves survives.
-#}
{%- set deny = (settings.get('permissions', {}).get('deny', [])
      | union(shipped.get('permissions', {}).get('deny', [])) | sort) -%}
{%- set base = settings | combine({'permissions':
      settings.get('permissions', {}) | combine({'deny': deny})}) -%}
{%- set out = {} -%}
{%- for event, matchers in base.get('hooks', {}).items() -%}
  {%- set kept = [] -%}
  {%- for m in matchers -%}
    {%- set entries = m.hooks | default([])
        | rejectattr('command', 'defined')
        | list
      + m.hooks | default([])
        | selectattr('command', 'defined')
        | rejectattr('command', 'search', 'faramir-guard')
        | list -%}
    {%- if entries -%}{%- set _ = kept.append(m | combine({'hooks': entries})) -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if kept -%}{%- set _ = out.update({event: kept}) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if out -%}
{{ base | combine({'hooks': out}) | to_nice_json(indent=2) }}
{%- else -%}
{{ dict(base | dict2items | rejectattr('key', 'eq', 'hooks') | list | items2dict) | to_nice_json(indent=2) }}
{%- endif -%}
